   "text": "This SMILES was read from the drawing by hand. The lauroyl chain length and most of the stereocentres are partly guesses.\n\n**Reading, N-terminus to C-terminus:**\n- Ac-Arg, with the guanidine drawn as an acetylated arginine side chain.\n- A penicillamine, Pen1, whose gem-dimethyl carbon carries one sulfur of the disulfide.\n- Asn, Thr, then 7-methyl-Trp, then Lys(NHAc).\n- A second penicillamine, Pen2, which closes the macrocycle through the S\u2013S bond.\n- Tyr with a 2-aminoethoxy group on the phenol oxygen.\n- 2-Naphthylalanine.\n- A 4-aminotetrahydropyran-4-carboxylic acid residue, drawn as a quaternary carbon in a six-membered ring containing O.\n- Lys, with the side-chain amine acylated by two AEEA (\u2013CO\u2013CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013NH\u2013) units. These lead to \u03b3-Glu, whose \u03b1-amine is acylated by a lauroyl group (12 carbons, as best I could count).\n- Asn, then 3-pyridylalanine, then an N-methylglycinamide (sarcosinamide) C-terminus.\n\n**Uncertain points:**\n- **Lauroyl chain:** my count of the zigzag was 11 or 12 carbons, and I chose 12 (dodecanoyl).\n- **Stereochemistry:** I could not resolve every wedge and hash. Most centres are written as L, and the Lys carrying the linker and the naphthylalanine are written as D.\n\nSMILES: CC(=O)N[C@@H](CCCNC(N)=N)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)(C)S1)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2c[nH]c3c(C)cccc23)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCNC(C)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)(C)S1)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1ccc(OCCN)cc1)C(=O)N[C@H](Cc1ccc2ccccc2c1)C(=O)NC1(CCOCC1)C(=O)N[C@H](CCCCNC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)CC[C@H](NC(=O)CCCCCCCCCCC)C(=O)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1cccnc1)C(=O)N(C)CC(N)=O"
